# All Tenses Cheat Sheet

**Key:** `S` = subject, `V1` = base verb, `V2` = past form, `V3` = past participle, `V-ing` = verb + ing

---

## Present

| Tense | Form (+ / - / ?) | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Simple** | S + V1<br>S + do/does not + V1<br>Do/Does + S + V1? | Facts, habits, with frequency adverbs | She does yoga. |
| **Continuous** | S + am/is/are + V-ing<br>S + am/is/are not + V-ing<br>Am/Is/Are + S + V-ing? | Happening now, temporary actions, future plans | I am reading a book now. |
| **Perfect** | S + have/has + V3<br>S + have/has not + V3<br>Have/Has + S + V3? | Recent actions, no detail, "already/just/yet", "for/since" | She has gone to the market. |
| **Perfect Continuous** | S + have/has + been + V-ing<br>S + have/has not been + V-ing<br>Have/Has + S + been + V-ing? | Began in past, still going on ("for/since") | I have been teaching for 3 years. |

## Past

| Tense | Form (+ / - / ?) | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Simple** | S + V2<br>S + did not + V1<br>Did + S + V1? | Completed past actions, past facts | She cleaned her house yesterday. |
| **Continuous** | S + was/were + V-ing<br>S + was/were not + V-ing<br>Was/Were + S + V-ing? | In progress at a past time, interrupted action | I was watching TV at 7:00 last night. |
| **Perfect** | S + had + V3<br>S + had not + V3<br>Had + S + V3? | Action before another past action | She had eaten when he arrived. |
| **Perfect Continuous** | S + had been + V-ing<br>S + had not been + V-ing<br>Had + S + been + V-ing? | Began earlier in the past, continued to a past time | I had been working before we married. |

## Future

| Tense | Form (+ / - / ?) | Use | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Simple** | S + will + V1<br>S + will not + V1<br>Will + S + V1? | Fixed future, predictions, promises, decisions, offers | I will be 10 next year. |
| **Continuous** | S + will be + V-ing<br>S + will not be + V-ing<br>Will + S + be + V-ing? | In progress at a future time | I will be enjoying the sea. |
| **Perfect** | S + will have + V3<br>S + will not have + V3<br>Will + S + have + V3? | Completed before a future time | She will have finished school by then. |
| **Perfect Continuous** | S + will have been + V-ing<br>S + will not have been + V-ing<br>Will + S + have been + V-ing? | Begins earlier, continues to a future time | I will have been flying to New York by 12:00. |

---

## Quick Tips

- **Simple:** what happens or happened (fact, habit, completed).
- **Continuous:** what is/was/will be in progress.
- **Perfect:** what is done before a point in time.
- **Perfect Continuous:** how long something has been going on up to a point.
